From 4ba3396411c0a7e440d2b03c800e4b288359049d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:29:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] virtio/gpu: implement SET_SCANOUT_BLOB and drain the
 cursor queue

v1.19.6 panics the VMM on SET_SCANOUT_BLOB, which the guest's KMS driver
sends for every blob framebuffer: dumb buffers when virgl is not
negotiated, udmabufs, and the Venus images a DRM compositor such as
gamescope exports as dma-bufs and scans out.

Record the blob scanout's layout (offset of the visible rectangle and row
stride, validated against the framebuffer and the blob size) and, on
RESOURCE_FLUSH, copy its rows into the display backend's frame: from the
guest pages of blobs with guest storage, or on macOS from the blob's shm
mapping. virglrenderer backs every exportable Venus allocation with shm,
device-local or not, so the pixels the GPU rendered are readable there
once the guest's fence for that work has signaled. The display backend is
now reconfigured only when a scanout's size or format changes, not on every
page flip between same-sized buffers. A missing previously-scanned-out
resource no longer makes SET_SCANOUT fail.

The cursor queue was never serviced: once its 256 entries were used, the
guest driver blocked in virtio_gpu_queue_cursor() and with it every atomic
commit that moved the cursor plane. Complete cursor commands on their own
thread (the display API has no cursor; the host shows its own pointer).

CREATE_GUEST_HANDLE blobs (never negotiated) now fail with
ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER instead of a panic.
